The test exercises `_build_request` in four cases: normal builder with `get_updates=False`, normal builder with `get_updates=True`, and two override cases where `request` or `get_updates_request` is already set. In `_build_request`, `get_updates` is first read to define `prefix`, then read again in the early-return condition and later branch conditions. `prefix` is used in each `getattr(self, f"{prefix}...")` access and in the early return. In the non-override calls, the function continues to define `proxy`, `socket_options`, `connection_pool_size`, `timeouts`, `effective_timeouts`, and `http_version`, and those values are then read in the final `HTTPXRequest(...)` call or while computing `effective_timeouts`. In the override calls, execution returns at line 227, so only the early `get_updates`/`prefix` uses are observed there.

